}

{
  "summary": "The search-indexer is experiencing elevated timeout rates due to attempting to connect to the legacy port 9200, which has been moved to 9250. The service is still configured to use the old port, and stack traces confirm connection timeouts on 9200. The kafka-clickstream is healthy and not the root cause. All failed requests are hitting the timeout ceiling, indicating a misconfiguration in the upstream port setting for search-indexer."
}

{
  "summary": "The billing-cron service is experiencing elevated timeout rates due to connection attempts on the outdated port 5432, while the database listener has been moved to port 7432. The invoice-pdf-worker is healthy and not the cause. Stack traces and latency metrics confirm that all failed requests are timing out at the old port, indicating a misconfiguration in billing-cron's upstream port setting."
}

{
  "summary": "The notification-hub is experiencing elevated timeout rates due to attempting to connect to the legacy plaintext port 6379, which has been moved to TLS port 6380 in the valkey-pubsub cluster. The stack trace confirms connection timeouts on the old port, and the latency histogram shows all failed requests hitting the timeout ceiling. The smtp-relay-proxy is healthy and not the cause."
}

{
  "summary": "The analytics-etl service is experiencing elevated timeout rates due to connection attempts on the outdated HTTP port 8123, which was recently moved to port 9009 by the protocol upgrade CH-715. The service is still configured to use port 8123, leading to timeouts. The s3-parquet-sink is healthy and not the root cause. The stack trace confirms the timeout issue is originating from the analytics-etl service's connection to the upstream service on the incorrect port. The latency histogram shows all failed requests hitting the timeout ceiling, reinforcing the connection issue."
}

{
  "summary": "The Order-fulfillment service is experiencing elevated timeout rates due to a misconfiguration where it is still attempting to connect to the legacy port 5432, while the upstream service has been moved to port 15432. The stack trace confirms connection timeouts on the old port, and the latency histogram shows all failed requests hitting the timeout ceiling. The memcache-shipping-rates service is healthy and not the root cause."
